{
  "frames_scored": 30,
  "verdict": "Persistence WINS at every horizon. Constant-velocity advection is -8.4% IoU at T+1, -7.9% at T+2 and -7.7% at T+3. The shape of the failure says why: recall is unchanged to four decimals (0.4889 vs 0.4890) while precision falls 0.595 -> 0.517. Advection is not finding cells it was missing, it is moving correct cells to wrong places. That follows directly from the motion classifier's measured precision of 0.56 (eval_motion_separation.py): roughly two in five advected clusters were never moving, so they are carried off static structure they were correctly sitting on. Fixing the forecaster means fixing the motion labels first, not tuning the advection. Reported as the negative result it is: these numbers are the floor a learned world model has to beat, and the floor is persistence.",
